## Executive Summary

Claude Fable 5.1 is Anthropic's general-availability Mythos-tier model from their Claude family, released September 1, 2026, designed for complex, long-running agentic work, coding, and knowledge work. It features a massive 1M token context window, competitive pricing ($10/$50 per 1M tokens), and exceptional performance on agentic benchmarks (52.6% on Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1, 73.4% on CursorBench 3.2, 77.8% on Toolathon-Verified, 89.1% on SWE Multilingual, 67.4% on DeepSWE). Fable 5.1 ranks #1 on the RSI Index (35.03%), the highest score among all models, and costs 21% less than Claude Opus 5 ($1,481 vs $1,886). The model shares the same underlying architecture with Claude Mythos 5.1 but includes additional safeguards for general availability. The model was released alongside Claude Mythos 5.1, offering the same capabilities with different safety configurations.

---

## Model Identity and Background

**Developer:** Anthropic
**Release Date:** September 1, 2026
**Series:** Claude Fable (Fable 5.1, Mythos 5.1)
**Predecessor:** Claude Fable 5 (June 9, 2026)
**Successor:** Claude Opus 5.5 (September 22, 2026)
**License:** Proprietary
**Context Window:** 1,000,000 tokens
**Max Output:** 128,000 tokens

Claude Fable 5.1 is Anthropic's general-availability Mythos-tier model from their Claude family, released September 1, 2026. It shares the same underlying model architecture with Claude Mythos 5.1 but includes additional safety guardrails for high-risk cybersecurity, biology, chemistry, and distillation requests. Fable 5.1 was released alongside Claude Mythos 5.1 as part of Anthropic's split strategy, where the same underlying model is offered in two versions: Fable 5.1 (public, with safeguards) and Mythos 5.1 (restricted, with reduced safeguards). The model ranks #1 on the RSI Index (35.03%), the highest score among all models, and costs 21% less than Claude Opus 5 ($1,481 vs $1,886).

