### Cost Efficiency Analysis
**Source:** Multiple sources
**Snapshot:** 2026

Claude Fable 5.1's real cost efficiency depends on:
- Prompt caching usage (75% cost reduction on input tokens)
- Batch API usage (50% discount on input and output)
- Effort level selection (higher effort = more thinking tokens = higher cost)
- Task complexity and length
- Context length (1M tokens)

The model is positioned as Anthropic's general-availability Mythos-tier model, priced at $10/$50 per 1M tokens. The cache-read pricing dropped 75% compared to Fable 5 ($0.25 vs $1 per 1M tokens), cutting typical workload costs by approximately 25% and highly agentic workloads by up to 45%.

